---A deal represents a segment of inventory for displaying ads that contains the terms and targeting information that is used for serving as well as the deal stats and status. Note: A proposal may contain multiple deals.
---@class gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.Deal
---@field deliveryControl? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.DeliveryControl Output only. Specifies the pacing set by the publisher.
---@field privateAuctionTerms? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.PrivateAuctionTerms The terms for private auction deals.
---@field buyer? string Output only. Refers to a buyer in Real-time Bidding API's Buyer resource. Format: `buyers/{buyerAccountId}`
---@field buyerPermissionType? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.DealBuyerPermissionTypeEnum|string Output only. The buyer permission type of the deal.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time of the deal creation.
---@field publisherProfile? string Immutable. Reference to the seller on the deal. Format: `buyers/{buyerAccountId}/publisherProfiles/{publisherProfileId}`
---@field dealType? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.DealDealTypeEnum|string Output only. Type of deal.
---@field eligibleSeatIds? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.StringList Output only. If set, this field contains the list of DSP specific seat ids set by media planners that are eligible to transact on this deal. The seat ID is in the calling DSP's namespace.
---@field displayName? string Output only. The name of the deal. Maximum length of 255 unicode characters is allowed. Control characters are not allowed. Buyers cannot update this field. Note: Not to be confused with name, which is a unique identifier of the deal.
---@field billedBuyer? string Output only. When the client field is populated, this field refers to the buyer who creates and manages the client buyer and gets billed on behalf of the client buyer; when the buyer field is populated, this field is the same value as buyer; when the deal belongs to a media planner account, this field will be empty. Format : `buyers/{buyerAccountId}`
---@field name? string Immutable. The unique identifier of the deal. Auto-generated by the server when a deal is created. Format: buyers/{accountId}/proposals/{proposalId}/deals/{dealId}
---@field programmaticGuaranteedTerms? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.ProgrammaticGuaranteedTerms The terms for programmatic guaranteed deals.
---@field proposalRevision? string Output only. The revision number for the proposal and is the same value as proposal.proposal_revision. Each update to deal causes the proposal revision number to auto-increment. The buyer keeps track of the last revision number they know of and pass it in when making an update. If the head revision number on the server has since incremented, then an ABORTED error is returned during the update operation to let the buyer know that a subsequent update was made.
---@field client? string Output only. Refers to a Client. Format: `buyers/{buyerAccountId}/clients/{clientAccountid}`
---@field preferredDealTerms? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.PreferredDealTerms The terms for preferred deals.
---@field sellerTimeZone? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.TimeZone Output only. Time zone of the seller used to mark the boundaries of a day for daypart targeting and CPD billing.
---@field estimatedGrossSpend? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.Money Specified by buyers in request for proposal (RFP) to notify publisher the total estimated spend for the proposal. Publishers will receive this information and send back proposed deals accordingly.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time when the deal was last updated.
---@field mediaPlanner? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.MediaPlanner Output only. Refers to a buyer in Real-time Bidding API's Buyer resource. This field represents a media planner (For example, agency or big advertiser).
---@field flightStartTime? string Proposed flight start time of the deal. This will generally be stored in the granularity of one second since deal serving starts at seconds boundary. Any time specified with more granularity (for example, in milliseconds) will be truncated towards the start of time in seconds.
---@field flightEndTime? string Proposed flight end time of the deal. This will generally be stored in a granularity of a second. A value is not necessary for Private Auction deals.
---@field description? string Output only. Free text description for the deal terms.
---@field targeting? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.MarketplaceTargeting Specifies the subset of inventory targeted by the deal. Can be updated by the buyer before the deal is finalized.
---@field creativeRequirements? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.CreativeRequirements Output only. Metadata about the creatives of this deal.

---@alias gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.DealBuyerPermissionTypeEnum "BUYER_PERMISSION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NEGOTIATOR_ONLY"|"BIDDER"

---@alias gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.DealDealTypeEnum "DEAL_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PREFERRED_DEAL"|"PRIVATE_AUCTION"|"PROGRAMMATIC_GUARANTEED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.DealList gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.Deal[]

