---Mobile application targeting settings.
---@class gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.MobileApplicationTargeting
---@field firstPartyTargeting? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.FirstPartyMobileApplicationTargeting Publisher owned apps to be targeted or excluded by the publisher to display the ads in.

---Represents an amount of money with its currency type.
---@class gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.Money
---@field units? string The whole units of the amount. For example if `currencyCode` is `"USD"`, then 1 unit is one US dollar.
---@field currencyCode? string The three-letter currency code defined in ISO 4217.
---@field nanos? number Number of nano (10^-9) units of the amount. The value must be between -999,999,999 and +999,999,999 inclusive. If `units` is positive, `nanos` must be positive or zero. If `units` is zero, `nanos` can be positive, zero, or negative. If `units` is negative, `nanos` must be negative or zero. For example $-1.75 is represented as `units`=-1 and `nanos`=-750,000,000.

---A text note attached to the proposal to facilitate the communication between buyers and sellers.
---@class gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.Note
---@field createTime? string Output only. When this note was created.
---@field creatorRole? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.NoteCreatorRoleEnum|string Output only. The role who created the note.
---@field note? string The text of the note. Maximum length is 1024 characters.

---@alias gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.NoteCreatorRoleEnum "BUYER_SELLER_ROLE_UNSPECIFIED"|"BUYER"|"SELLER"

---@alias gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.NoteList gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.Note[]

---Represents targeting information for operating systems.
---@class gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.OperatingSystemTargeting
