---@class gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.PatchBuyersClientsRequest
---@field displayName? string Required. Display name shown to publishers. Must be unique for clients without partnerClientId specified. Maximum length of 255 characters is allowed.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.ClientStateEnum|string Output only. The state of the client.
---@field partnerClientId? string Arbitrary unique identifier provided by the buyer. This field can be used to associate a client with an identifier in the namespace of the buyer, lookup clients by that identifier and verify whether an Authorized Buyers account of the client already exists. If present, must be unique across all the clients.
---@field sellerVisible? boolean Whether the client will be visible to sellers.
---@field role? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.ClientRoleEnum|string Required. The role assigned to the client. Each role implies a set of permissions granted to the client.
---@field updateMask? string List of fields to be updated. If empty or unspecified, the service will update all fields populated in the update request excluding the output only fields and primitive fields with default value. Note that explicit field mask is required in order to reset a primitive field back to its default value, for example, false for boolean fields, 0 for integer fields. A special field mask consisting of a single path "*" can be used to indicate full replacement(the equivalent of PUT method), updatable fields unset or unspecified in the input will be cleared or set to default value. Output only fields will be ignored regardless of the value of updateMask.
---@field name string Output only. The resource name of the client. Format: `buyers/{accountId}/clients/{clientAccountId}`

---@class gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.PatchBuyersDataSegmentsRequest
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Time the data segment was last updated.
---@field userListId? string Optional. Immutable. The ID of the User List wrapped by this Data Segment. Curators with a linked Data Partner account can create a data segment that wraps a user list owned by the linked Data Partner account. User lists can be uploaded and managed using the [Data Manager API](https://developers.google.com/data-manager/api/data-partners/audiences). Linking a user list to a data segment lets you define a segment of inventory that is based on an audience you create.
---@field cpmFee? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.Money Optional. A fixed fee charged per thousand impressions. Once set, the currency code cannot be changed.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.DataSegmentStateEnum|string Output only. The state of the data segment.
---@field millipercentOfMediaFee? string Optional. The fee will be charged as a percentage of the impression cost, represented in millipercent. For example, 1% is represented as 1000.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time the data segment was created.
---@field updateMask? string Optional. List of fields to be updated. If empty or unspecified, the service will update all fields populated in the update request excluding the output only fields and primitive fields with default value. Note that explicit field mask is required in order to reset a primitive field back to its default value, for example, false for boolean fields, 0 for integer fields. A special field mask consisting of a single path "*" can be used to indicate full replacement(the equivalent of PUT method), updatable fields unset or unspecified in the input will be cleared or set to default value. Output only fields will be ignored regardless of the value of updateMask.
---@field name string Immutable. Identifier. The unique identifier for the data segment. Account ID corresponds to the account ID that created the segment. v1alpha format: `buyers/{accountId}/dataSegments/{curatorDataSegmentId}` v1beta format: `curators/{curatorAccountId}/dataSegments/{curatorDataSegmentId}`

---@class gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.PatchBuyersProposalsDealsRequest
---@field deliveryControl? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.DeliveryControl Output only. Specifies the pacing set by the publisher.
---@field privateAuctionTerms? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.PrivateAuctionTerms The terms for private auction deals.
---@field buyer? string Output only. Refers to a buyer in Real-time Bidding API's Buyer resource. Format: `buyers/{buyerAccountId}`
---@field buyerPermissionType? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.DealBuyerPermissionTypeEnum|string Output only. The buyer permission type of the deal.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time of the deal creation.
---@field publisherProfile? string Immutable. Reference to the seller on the deal. Format: `buyers/{buyerAccountId}/publisherProfiles/{publisherProfileId}`
---@field dealType? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.DealDealTypeEnum|string Output only. Type of deal.
---@field eligibleSeatIds? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.StringList Output only. If set, this field contains the list of DSP specific seat ids set by media planners that are eligible to transact on this deal. The seat ID is in the calling DSP's namespace.
---@field displayName? string Output only. The name of the deal. Maximum length of 255 unicode characters is allowed. Control characters are not allowed. Buyers cannot update this field. Note: Not to be confused with name, which is a unique identifier of the deal.
---@field billedBuyer? string Output only. When the client field is populated, this field refers to the buyer who creates and manages the client buyer and gets billed on behalf of the client buyer; when the buyer field is populated, this field is the same value as buyer; when the deal belongs to a media planner account, this field will be empty. Format : `buyers/{buyerAccountId}`
---@field programmaticGuaranteedTerms? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.ProgrammaticGuaranteedTerms The terms for programmatic guaranteed deals.
---@field proposalRevision? string Output only. The revision number for the proposal and is the same value as proposal.proposal_revision. Each update to deal causes the proposal revision number to auto-increment. The buyer keeps track of the last revision number they know of and pass it in when making an update. If the head revision number on the server has since incremented, then an ABORTED error is returned during the update operation to let the buyer know that a subsequent update was made.
---@field client? string Output only. Refers to a Client. Format: `buyers/{buyerAccountId}/clients/{clientAccountid}`
---@field preferredDealTerms? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.PreferredDealTerms The terms for preferred deals.
---@field sellerTimeZone? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.TimeZone Output only. Time zone of the seller used to mark the boundaries of a day for daypart targeting and CPD billing.
---@field estimatedGrossSpend? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.Money Specified by buyers in request for proposal (RFP) to notify publisher the total estimated spend for the proposal. Publishers will receive this information and send back proposed deals accordingly.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time when the deal was last updated.
---@field mediaPlanner? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.MediaPlanner Output only. Refers to a buyer in Real-time Bidding API's Buyer resource. This field represents a media planner (For example, agency or big advertiser).
---@field flightStartTime? string Proposed flight start time of the deal. This will generally be stored in the granularity of one second since deal serving starts at seconds boundary. Any time specified with more granularity (for example, in milliseconds) will be truncated towards the start of time in seconds.
---@field flightEndTime? string Proposed flight end time of the deal. This will generally be stored in a granularity of a second. A value is not necessary for Private Auction deals.
---@field description? string Output only. Free text description for the deal terms.
---@field targeting? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.MarketplaceTargeting Specifies the subset of inventory targeted by the deal. Can be updated by the buyer before the deal is finalized.
---@field creativeRequirements? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.CreativeRequirements Output only. Metadata about the creatives of this deal.
---@field name string Immutable. The unique identifier of the deal. Auto-generated by the server when a deal is created. Format: buyers/{accountId}/proposals/{proposalId}/deals/{dealId}
---@field updateMask? string List of fields to be updated. If empty or unspecified, the service will update all fields populated in the update request excluding the output only fields and primitive fields with default value. Note that explicit field mask is required in order to reset a primitive field back to its default value, for example, false for boolean fields, 0 for integer fields. A special field mask consisting of a single path "*" can be used to indicate full replacement(the equivalent of PUT method), updatable fields unset or unspecified in the input will be cleared or set to default value. Output only fields will be ignored regardless of the value of updateMask.

---@class gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.PatchBuyersProposalsRequest
---@field dealType? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.ProposalDealTypeEnum|string Output only. Type of deal the proposal contains.
---@field termsAndConditions? string Output only. The terms and conditions associated with this proposal. Accepting a proposal implies acceptance of this field. This is created by the seller, the buyer can only view it.
---@field displayName? string Output only. The descriptive name for the proposal. Maximum length of 255 unicode characters is allowed. Control characters are not allowed. Buyers cannot update this field. Note: Not to be confused with name, which is a unique identifier of the proposal.
---@field billedBuyer? string Output only. When the client field is populated, this field refers to the buyer who creates and manages the client buyer and gets billed on behalf of the client buyer; when the buyer field is populated, this field is the same value as buyer. Format : `buyers/{buyerAccountId}`
---@field buyerContacts? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.ContactList Contact information for the buyer.
---@field notes? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.NoteList A list of notes from the buyer and the seller attached to this proposal.
---@field sellerContacts? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.ContactList Output only. Contact information for the seller.
---@field originatorRole? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.ProposalOriginatorRoleEnum|string Output only. Indicates whether the buyer/seller created the proposal.
---@field pausingConsented? boolean Whether pausing is allowed for the proposal. This is a negotiable term between buyers and publishers.
---@field buyer? string Output only. Refers to a buyer in The Realtime-bidding API. Format: `buyers/{buyerAccountId}`
---@field isRenegotiating? boolean Output only. True if the proposal was previously finalized and is now being renegotiated.
---@field lastUpdaterOrCommentorRole? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.ProposalLastUpdaterOrCommentorRoleEnum|string Output only. The role of the last user that either updated the proposal or left a comment.
---@field proposalRevision? string Output only. The revision number for the proposal. Each update to the proposal or deal causes the proposal revision number to auto-increment. The buyer keeps track of the last revision number they know of and pass it in when making an update. If the head revision number on the server has since incremented, then an ABORTED error is returned during the update operation to let the buyer know that a subsequent update was made.
---@field client? string Output only. Refers to a Client. Format: `buyers/{buyerAccountId}/clients/{clientAccountid}`
---@field buyerPrivateData? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.PrivateData Buyer private data (hidden from seller).
---@field state? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.ProposalStateEnum|string Output only. Indicates the state of the proposal.
---@field publisherProfile? string Immutable. Reference to the seller on the proposal. Format: `buyers/{buyerAccountId}/publisherProfiles/{publisherProfileId}` Note: This field may be set only when creating the resource. Modifying this field while updating the resource will result in an error.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time when the proposal was last revised.
---@field name string Immutable. The name of the proposal serving as a unique identifier. Format: buyers/{accountId}/proposals/{proposalId}
---@field updateMask? string List of fields to be updated. If empty or unspecified, the service will update all fields populated in the update request excluding the output only fields and primitive fields with default value. Note that explicit field mask is required in order to reset a primitive field back to its default value, for example, false for boolean fields, 0 for integer fields. A special field mask consisting of a single path "*" can be used to indicate full replacement(the equivalent of PUT method), updatable fields unset or unspecified in the input will be cleared or set to default value. Output only fields will be ignored regardless of the value of updateMask.

---@class gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.PatchCuratorsCuratedPackagesRequest
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name assigned to the curated package by the curator. Can be used to filter the response of the curatedPackages.list method.
---@field feeCpm? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.Money Optional. The CPM fee charged by the curator to buyers using this curated package. Can be used to filter the response of the curatedPackages.list method.
---@field curationFeeVisibility? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.CuratedPackageCurationFeeVisibilityEnum|string Optional. Immutable. The visibility of the combined curation package fee and data segment fees (the total curation fee).
---@field targeting? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.PackageTargeting Optional. Targeting criteria for the curated package.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the curated package was last updated. Can be used to filter the response of the curatedPackages.list method.
---@field floorPriceCpm? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.Money Optional. The minimum CPM a buyer has to bid to participate in auctions for inventory in this curated package. Can be used to filter the response of the curatedPackages.list method.
---@field accessSettings? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.AccessControlSettings Required. Settings for controlling access to the curated package. Access to this curated package is limited to the allowlisted media planners and the creator. Buyers and bidders can not be allowlisted for or have direct access to this resource.
---@field description? string Optional. A description of the curated package, provided by the curator.
---@field millipercentOfMediaFee? string Optional. The fee will be charged as a percentage of the impression cost, represented in millipercent. For example, 1% is represented as 1000.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1alpha.CuratedPackageStateEnum|string Output only. The state of the curated package. Can be used to filter the response of the curatedPackages.list method.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the curated package was created. Can be used to filter the response of the curatedPackages.list method.
---@field name string Identifier. The unique resource name for the curated package. Format: `curators/{accountId}/curatedPackages/{curatedPackageId}`
---@field updateMask? string Optional. List of fields to be updated. If empty or unspecified, the service will update all fields populated in the update request excluding the output only fields and primitive fields with default value. Note that explicit field mask is required in order to reset a primitive field back to its default value, for example, false for boolean fields, 0 for integer fields. A special field mask consisting of a single path "*" can be used to indicate full replacement (the equivalent of PUT method), updatable fields unset or unspecified in the input will be cleared or set to default value. Output only fields will be ignored regardless of the value of updateMask.

